# The 22-package floor (01-boot-layer.md §2), as direct dependencies — apt resolves the
# closure, and `--apt-recommends false` keeps it from widening.
#
# This is the irreducible floor for any KMS GUI, not Slint's overhead: libinput, libseat,
# libxkbcommon, freetype, fontconfig, fonts-dejavu and their closure, at 21 MiB. The
# competing measurement was Tauri at 268 packages / 650 MiB
# (docs/research/05-tauri-viability.md).
#
# The published package manifest (ADR-0012) is what makes this auditable without
# building the image.

# Slint on backend-linuxkms + renderer-software. No X server, no Wayland compositor, no
# cage, no display manager, no GPU driver.
libinput10
libseat1
libxkbcommon0
libfontconfig1
libfreetype6
fonts-dejavu-core

# seatd, 104 KiB, with LIBSEAT_BACKEND=seatd. greetd is rejected: its initial_session
# runs exactly once per boot by design, which is the opposite of what a restarting kiosk
# needs.
seatd

# Deliberately absent, each for a reason recorded in the spec:
#
#   network-manager   §3 — 7.6 MiB, and worthless as a guarantee on its own
#   firmware-*        §3 — no network driver gets firmware because none is installed
#   udisks2, gvfs     §4 — nothing exists to mount anything
#   kdump-tools       §4 — no kernel crash dumps
#   v4l-utils         §7 — the app talks V4L2 ioctls directly
#   libv4l-0t64       §7 — same
#   any terminal emulator, SSH server or getty
#                     §2 — nothing here is meant to be driven from a shell, so one is
#                          only a mistake surface, and it advertises a capability the
#                          appliance does not offer
